# EventBus Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph EventBus
        direction LR
        NQ[nextQueue<br/>Deferred events accumulate]
        CQ[currentQueue<br/>Events being processed]
    end

    S1[System A] -->|Emit Deferred| NQ
    S2[System B] -->|Emit Immediate| IH[Immediate Handler]

    subgraph Tick Lifecycle
        direction TB
        AT[1. AdvanceTick<br/>nextQueue → currentQueue] --> TE[2. Systems Execute<br/>May emit events to nextQueue]
        TE --> FL[3. Flush<br/>Dispatch currentQueue to handlers]
        FL --> NE[4. Events emitted during Flush<br/>Go to nextQueue for next tick]
    end

    NQ -->|AdvanceTick| CQ
    CQ -->|Flush| H1[Handler 1]
    CQ -->|Flush| H2[Handler 2]
    CQ -->|Flush| H3[Handler N]

    IH --> SH[System Handler]

    style NQ fill:#4a9eff,color:#fff
    style CQ fill:#ff6b4a,color:#fff
    style AT fill:#2d8f2d,color:#fff
    style FL fill:#8f2d2d,color:#fff
```

## Queue Swap Animation

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Engine
    participant EventBus
    participant Systems
    participant Handlers

    Engine->>EventBus: AdvanceTick()
    Note over EventBus: Swap queues<br/>nextQueue → currentQueue<br/>Clear old currentQueue

    Engine->>Systems: ExecuteAll()
    Systems->>EventBus: Emit Deferred → nextQueue
    Systems->>EventBus: Emit Immediate → Handlers

    Engine->>EventBus: Flush()
    EventBus->>Handlers: Process currentQueue events
    Note over EventBus: Events emitted during Flush<br/>go to nextQueue
```

## Dispatch Types

| Type | When | Processing |
|------|------|------------|
| Deferred | Default for all events | Queued in nextQueue, processed next tick |
| Immediate | Fatal errors only (FatalError, EngineShutdown) | Processed inline at emit time |

## Rules

1. Deferred events accumulate in `nextQueue` and process in the following tick
2. Immediate events process immediately (fatal errors only)
3. A System cannot read the result of its own event in the same tick
4. A System may emit multiple events per tick
5. Events are processed in FIFO order
6. Events emitted during `Flush` go to `nextQueue`, not the current `currentQueue`
7. Max 10,000 events per tick (configurable). Excess discarded with overflow flag
